{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'ls -l gate-run3* mutants* render*; cat mutants.log; cat gate-run3.txt'","aggregated_output":"-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   88456 Nov 22 13:25 gate-run3.fixtures.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    5592 Nov 22 13:25 gate-run3.txt\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     570 Nov 22 13:26 mutants.log\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    3750 Nov 22 13:26 mutants.py\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff   12035 Nov 22 13:26 render-r1.answer.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  148733 Nov 22 13:26 render-r1.request.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     320 Nov 22 13:26 render-r1.txt\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    9919 Nov 22 13:26 render_v13.py\nmutant | expected miss | result\ncontrol (unmutated) | none | PASS (none)\nC4 path rule off | R1b | CAUGHT (['R1b'])\nC3 off | R1a | CAUGHT (['R1a'])\nC1 accepts any substring (alone) | T9 | CAUGHT (['T9'])\nC5 allows estimates | P3b | CAUGHT (['P3b'])\nper-unit identity ignores scope | P4 | CAUGHT (['P4'])\nper-unit inverse loses its scale | G3inv | CAUGHT (['G3inv'])\nC2 tolerance 50% | P2 | CAUGHT (['P2', 'U2'])\nbound direction ignored | R4m | CAUGHT (['R4m'])\nC9 same base off (both clauses) | G4m | CAUGHT (['G4m'])\nC10 prior not authenticated | P3c | CAUGHT (['P3c'])\njudging-v13 $0 gate (DESIGN.md v5 §6)\n\nPASS  R1a    C3 on Q4\n        C5: v9: the reference prior414 rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\n        C3: FY2027 Q4 base: v9 dcq4 (146.0–146.0) exceeds v14 q4f (127.1–127.1)\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: v9 reaches g3 without passing the forecast node q3f\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R1b    C4 on the Q3 bypass, no C3\n        C4: ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027 Q3') base: v9 reaches g3 without passing the forecast node q3f\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R1c    passes\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R2     overlap recorded; ~35 crosses 50\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"overlap\", \"figure\": \"end\", \"outcome\": \"v29\", \"value\": 53.0, \"alternate\": 35.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [50], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  R3a    C1 on both stripped qualifiers\n        C1: a730: \"$730 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e1786\n        C1: b800: \"$800 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e2535\n        C8: share45: converts a730, b800 to four largest AI hyperscalers combined CY2026 share of top-five capex with no bridge naming those operands\n        C8: cap27: converts c1300 to four largest AI hyperscalers combined CY2027 data-center capex with no bridge naming those operands\nPASS  R3b    passes C1, C8 without bridges\n        C8: share45: converts a730, b800 to four largest AI hyperscalers combined CY2026 share of top-five capex with no bridge naming those operands\n        C8: cap27: converts c1300 to four largest AI hyperscalers combined CY2027 data-center capex with no bridge naming those operands\nPASS  R3c    bridges recorded, undetermined\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"share45\", \"bridge\": \"br1\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"cap27\", \"bridge\": \"br2\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  R4     trim definitely crosses 40\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"vera28\", \"outcome\": \"v41\", \"value\": 38.5, \"alternate\": 40.0, \"alternate_bound\": \">\", \"boundaries_crossed\": [40], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G1     passes, estimates visible\nPASS  G2     passes, estimates visible\nPASS  G3     passes, estimates visible\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"gvera\", \"outcome\": \"v19\", \"value\": 13.0, \"alternate\": 20.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [20], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G4     passes, estimates visible\nPASS  P1     C1 only, on gq1\n        C1: gq1: value 81.9 USD bn bound None does not equal \"$81.6 billion\" as component value\nPASS  P2     C2 only, on gfy\n        C2: gfy: declared 450.0–480.0 but sum of ['gh1', 'gh2'] gives 400.60–434.60\nPASS  P3a    C5 only\n        C5: v1: the reference pri rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\nPASS  P3c    C10: a prior figure the earlier answer does not state\n        C5: v1: the reference pri rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\n        C10: pri: no earlier answer of v1 on 2026-07-13 shown in the request states 431.0\nPASS  P3b    C5 only\n        C5: v1: the reference wrap rests on the system's own forecast or an estimate\nPASS  P4     C8 only, on gunits: the per-unit identity needs one scope\n        C8: gunits: converts gt20, gasp to NVIDIA Vera CPU FY2027 units with no bridge naming those operands\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"gvera\", \"outcome\": \"v19\", \"value\": 13.0, \"alternate\": 20.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [20], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G3inv  the per-unit inverse gives $20B\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"gvera\", \"outcome\": \"v19\", \"value\": 13.0, \"alternate\": 20.0, \"alternate_bound\": null, \"boundaries_crossed\": [20], \"certainty\": \"definite\"}\nPASS  G4m    C9: FY2028 rests on consensus, not q01's forecast\n        C9: v22 does not rest on v1's forecast gfy\n        C9: v22 reaches gc392 for ('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'company', 'FY2027') without v1's forecast gfy\nPASS  R4m    C2: the bound direction reversed\n        C2: cpu28: its inputs make it a lower bound, but it is declared <\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"adjustment\", \"figure\": \"vera28\", \"outcome\": \"v41\", \"value\": 38.5, \"alternate\": 40.0, \"alternate_bound\": \"<\", \"boundaries_crossed\": [40], \"certainty\": \"possible\"}\nPASS  T1     accepted\nPASS  T2     accepted\nPASS  T3a    accepted\nPASS  T3b    accepted\nPASS  T4     accepted\nPASS  T5a    refused\n        C1: t: \"$730 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e1786\nPASS  T5b    refused\n        C1: t: \"$800 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e2535\nPASS  T6     refused\n        C1: t: \"double\" is not a complete numeric expression of e3660\nPASS  T7     refused\n        C1: t: value 108.5 USD bn bound None does not equal \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\" as component midpoint\nPASS  T8     refused\n        C1: t: value 730.0 USD bn bound None does not equal \"more than $730 billion\" as component value\nPASS  T9     refused\n        C1: t: \"$800 billion\" is not a complete numeric expression of e2535\nPASS  U1     decision held\n        recorded: {\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}\nPASS  U2     two refusals give unresolved\n        C2: gfy: declared 450.0–480.0 but sum of ['gh1', 'gh2'] gives 400.60–434.60\n\n34 items, 34 pass, misses: none\nGATE PASS\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba REQUEST-AUDIT.md; nl -ba render_v13.py; rg -n 'C[0-9]|G4m|R4m|P3c|G3inv|T9|v7|\"'^##'\"' DESIGN.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# judging-v13 request audit (DESIGN.md §5; $0)\n     2\t\n     3\tThe system text is `judging-v13-draft.txt`: 4,835 characters, against judging-v7's 4,924 (−89). The format definitions sit in the schema\n     4\tdescriptions beside their fields (AGENTS §3, §6), not in the system text.\n     5\t\n     6\t## The system text, sentence by sentence against judging-v7\n     7\t\n     8\t| v7 sentence | v13 | Source |\n     9\t|---|---|---|\n    10\t| L1 \"judging a thesis's current rung … Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes\" | \"the current rungs of a family of related number theses …\"; dependency conclusions removed | D725 (the unit is a family); the family has no dependency reads |\n    11\t| L3 \"the current conclusions of dependencies\" | removed | the same |\n    12\t| L3 \"Pieces in force … are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them\" | \"each member's earlier forecast reflects them, but its figures are our own, never a source and never the market's expectation\" | D198 kept; the self-made reference (D693 trace, `self-reference/RESULT.md`); C5 |\n    13\t| L3 \"Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\" | kept, per member | D260 |\n    14\t| L4 reference, run-rate, shifts, product-target discount | kept word for word, per member | D260, D263 (the frozen gold's reasoning) |\n    15\t| L4 \"State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share)\" | \"Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario\" | D260 clause (3), made family-wide; C3, C4 |\n    16\t| L5 tiers, novelty, discounting, sizing, identities | kept word for word | D260, D263 |\n    17\t| L6 replacement | kept | D198 |\n    18\t| L7 themes | kept, per member | D191, D195 |\n    19\t| L8 dependencies \"not yet created\" or \"historical only\" | removed | a family has no dependency reads (`cites_views` always empty) |\n    20\t| L9 consistency with dependencies and themes; \"a component cannot exceed its whole\" | \"consistent with each other and with the themes in force\"; the component clause moved into L4's family sentence | D260; the duplicate removed (AGENTS §6) |\n    21\t| L10 the output list (one rung, reference, implied_outcome …) | \"Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge … is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved …\" | D725, DESIGN §2; field definitions moved to the schema |\n    22\t| L11 changed | kept | PRD 06 |\n    23\t\n    24\t**Read in both directions** (AGENTS §6):\n    25\t- No v13 sentence keeps wider or narrower than v7 on the standard.\n    26\t- The only new rules are the three D725 contracts: one calculation, figures labelled, and unresolved allowed. Code enforces each.\n    27\t- The product-target sentence (\"discounted by default\") is kept. D721 and Codex's round 43 found that the gold relies on it (q19).\n    28\t\n    29\t## The schema descriptions (the format's definitions, beside their fields)\n    30\t\n    31\t- **`figures[].what`:** \"What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue; never its basis), scope, period.\"\n    32\t- **`figures[].basis`:**\n    33\t  - reported: an actual;\n    34\t  - guidance: the company's outlook;\n    35\t  - consensus: analysts' average;\n    36\t  - third_party: one outside party;\n    37\t  - forecast: this family's forecast;\n    38\t  - prior_forecast: our earlier forecast, with its pointer.\n    39\t- **`figures[].kind`:**\n    40\t  - source: stated in a shown passage;\n    41\t  - computed: one operation on named figures;\n    42\t  - estimate: your judgement.\n    43\t- **`figures[].expression`, source only:** \"the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes it, qualifiers included (for\n    44\t  example 'more than $2 billion', '$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%', 'more than triple')\". The examples come from no gate case [46f.4].\n    45\t- **`figures[].relation`, sum and roll_forward:**\n    46\t  - time_aggregation: periods of one quantity;\n    47\t  - accounting_parts: declared parts of a whole;\n    48\t  - stated_in_addition: a source says the amounts add;\n    49\t  - overlap_unknown: name the disputed figure.\n    50\t- **`figures[].bridge`:** \"Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, declared parts, a balance and its\n    51\t  flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it\n    52\t  converts.\" This matches C8's operation-specific rules, so q01's quarters-to-half and q02's mix applied to consensus need none [46f.4].\n    53\t- **`figures[].adjusts`, estimate only:** \"The stated figure this estimate changes, and how: discount, uplift or trim.\"\n    54\t- **`answers[]`:**\n    55\t  - **forecast:** the outcome figure, and the rung whose band contains it or, for a range spanning several bands, the band you choose,\n    56\t    with the reason. The reference is an external figure, or a calculation from external and reported figures, or `unavailable` with\n    57\t    why. It is never our earlier forecast.\n    58\t  - **unresolved:** why.\n    59\t\n    60\t## The family header (user message, before the evidence)\n    61\t\n    62\t`[Family] members: <id> (<question>, ladder …) …`, then:\n    63\t- `Relations: <part> is part of <whole>; <later> rests on <earlier>'s base.`\n    64\t- `Shared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: <population, measure, scope, period> …`\n    65\t\n    66\tThe family header, the members' earlier forecasts (labelled \"our earlier forecast, not a source\") and the union of evidence in view\n    67\tfollow the order of v7's request.\n    68\t\n    69\t## Earlier forecasts [46f.4]\n    70\t\n    71\tThe draft says the earlier forecasts are \"supplied only for comparison\", and C10 makes that a check: a `prior` figure feeds no figure.\n    72\tThe design's earlier clause allowing a dated prior to feed a `same_base` is withdrawn. A later year reads the earlier member's forecast\n    73\tnode in the same call (C9).\n    74\t\n    75\t## Rendered and checked (`render_v13.py`, `render-r1.*`)\n    76\t\n    77\t- **The request:** the old-2 family on 09-20 (calls 8729 and 8737). System text 4,835 characters; user message 123,304 characters, with\n    78\t  237 evidence items, the family header, the themes once and the earlier forecasts labelled; schema 10,066 characters.\n    79\t- **The answer:** the R1c control answer, in strict shape (every optional field null). It passes `model.check_schema` with no error and\n    80\t  calc_check with no error. Every passage it cites is in the rendered request.\n    81\t- **Tokens:** not counted here. The two v7 calls were 36,151 input tokens together (Codex, round 45b).\n    82\t\n    83\t## Not yet done\n    84\t\n    85\t- The product request builder (the harness renderer above is not it).\n    86\t- The sender for the paid gate.\n    87\t\n    88\tBoth are build work after the $0 gate.\n     1\t\"\"\"Render one stored family's judging-v13 request (old-2 calls 8729 and 8737 on 2026-09-20) and check a conforming answer through the\n     2\tv13 schema (model.check_schema) and calc_check. Harness-only, $0, no model call. Usage: python3 render_v13.py [out-prefix]\"\"\"\n     3\timport json\n     4\timport sqlite3\n     5\timport sys\n     6\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     7\t\n     8\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n     9\tREPO = HERE.parents[2]\n    10\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    11\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    12\timport calc_check as cc  # noqa: E402\n    13\timport gate  # noqa: E402\n    14\tfrom hivemind import model  # noqa: E402\n    15\t\n    16\tS, N = {'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'number'}\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef nullable(schema):\n    20\t    return {'anyOf': [schema, {'type': 'null'}]}\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef obj(props, desc=None):\n    24\t    out = {'type': 'object', 'properties': props, 'required': list(props), 'additionalProperties': False}\n    25\t    if desc:\n    26\t        out['description'] = desc\n    27\t    return out\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    31\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\n    32\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\n    33\t    figure = obj({\n    34\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\n    35\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s outlook; consensus: '\n    36\t                  'analysts\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\'s forecast; prior_forecast: our earlier forecast.'},\n    37\t        'scenario': S,\n    38\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.KINDS), 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one operation on '\n    39\t                 'named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours; prior: our earlier forecast, for comparison only.'},\n    40\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\n    41\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\n    42\t        'unit': S,\n    43\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\n    44\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\n    45\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\n    46\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\n    47\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    48\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\n    49\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\n    50\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\n    51\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\n    52\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\n    53\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\n    54\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\n    55\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\n    56\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\n    57\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    58\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\n    59\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    60\t        'pointer': nullable(obj({'view': S, 'day': S})),\n    61\t    })\n    62\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    63\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n    64\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    65\t    answer = obj({\n    66\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n    67\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n    68\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n    69\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n    70\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why; never our earlier forecast.')),\n    71\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n    72\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n    73\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    74\t        'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': S,\n    75\t    })\n    76\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef parts(user):\n    80\t    head, rest = user.split('\\n\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\n    81\t    evidence = '[Evidence in view' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0]\n    82\t    tail = '\\n\\n[' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[1] if '\\n\\n[' in rest else ''\n    83\t    blocks = {b.split(']', 1)[0]: '[' + b for b in tail.split('\\n\\n[')[1:]}\n    84\t    return head, evidence, blocks\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef render(archive_path, calls, family):\n    88\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    89\t    heads, lines, seen, themes, earlier = [], [], set(), '', []\n    90\t    for view_id, call_id in calls:\n    91\t        user = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\n    92\t        head, evidence, blocks = parts(user)\n    93\t        heads.append(head)\n    94\t        for item in evidence.split('\\n- ')[1:]:\n    95\t            eid = item.split(' ', 1)[0]\n    96\t            if eid not in seen:\n    97\t                seen.add(eid)\n    98\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\n    99\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\n   100\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '')\n   101\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\n   102\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\"part\"]} is part of {r[\"whole\"]}' for r in family['relations'] if r['type'] == 'part_of')\n   103\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family['shared'])\n   104\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n\\n'\n   105\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\n' + '\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n\\n' + themes + '\\n\\n[Earlier forecasts]\\n'\n   106\t            + '\\n'.join(earlier) + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')\n   107\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\n- ')[1:]]\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\tdef strict(calc, schema):\n   111\t    \"\"\"Fill every optional field with null, as strict structured output returns it.\"\"\"\n   112\t    fprops = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']\n   113\t    aprops = schema['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']\n   114\t    figs = [{k: f.get(k) for k in fprops} for f in calc['figures']]\n   115\t    for f in figs:\n   116\t        f['scenario'] = f['scenario'] or 'base'\n   117\t        if f['what'] is None:\n   118\t            f['what'] = {'population': '', 'measure': '', 'scope': '', 'period': ''}\n   119\t    answers = []\n   120\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   121\t        a2 = {k: a.get(k) for k in aprops}\n   122\t        if a2['reference'] is not None:\n   123\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': a['reference'].get('figure'), 'unavailable': a['reference'].get('unavailable')}\n   124\t        a2['why'] = a.get('why')\n   125\t        answers.append(a2)\n   126\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': answers}\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef without_nulls(calc):\n   130\t    clean = lambda d: {k: v for k, v in d.items() if v is not None}\n   131\t    answers = []\n   132\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   133\t        a2 = clean(a)\n   134\t        if 'reference' in a2:\n   135\t            a2['reference'] = clean(a2['reference'])\n   136\t        answers.append(a2)\n   137\t    return {'figures': [clean(f) for f in calc['figures']], 'answers': answers}\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\tdef main():\n   141\t    archive = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\n   142\t    system = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n   143\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = render(archive, [('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)], gate.R1_FAMILY)\n   144\t    schema = v13_schema(['v14', 'v9'], evidence_ids, theme_ids)\n   145\t    calc = gate.r1('c')\n   146\t    answer = strict(calc, schema)\n   147\t    schema_errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\n   148\t    for a in answer['answers']:\n   149\t        a['cites'] = [e for e in a['cites'] if e in evidence_ids]\n   150\t    result = cc.check(gate.R1_FAMILY, gate.R1_PASSAGES, without_nulls(answer))\n   151\t    missing = sorted({f['evidence'] for f in calc['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} - set(evidence_ids))\n   152\t    report = [f'system {len(system)} characters; user {len(user)} characters; schema {len(json.dumps(schema))} characters',\n   153\t              f'evidence items {len(evidence_ids)}; themes {len(theme_ids)}',\n   154\t              f'source passages the answer cites that the rendered request does not show: {missing or \"none\"}',\n   155\t              f'schema errors: {schema_errors or \"none\"}', f'calc_check errors: {result[\"errors\"] or \"none\"}',\n   156\t              f'recorded: {json.dumps(result[\"recorded\"])}']\n   157\t    print('\\n'.join(report))\n   158\t    if len(sys.argv) > 1:\n   159\t        prefix = Path(sys.argv[1])\n   160\t        prefix.with_suffix('.request.json').write_text(json.dumps({'system': system, 'user': user, 'schema': schema}, indent=1))\n   161\t        prefix.with_suffix('.answer.json').write_text(json.dumps(answer, indent=1))\n   162\t        prefix.with_suffix('.txt').write_text('\\n'.join(report) + '\\n')\n   163\t    return 0 if not schema_errors and not result['errors'] and not missing else 1\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   167\t    raise SystemExit(main())\n1:# judging-v13: related number questions judged together, with a checked calculation (design v7, after council round 46f; for round 46g)\n4:the ordinary launchers refuse it (D359, D723). The frozen judge (judging-v7, poc-v118) is unchanged.\n15:## 1. What changes\n17:| Piece | judging-v7 (today) | judging-v13 |\n24:| Request text | judging-v7 | a full v13 request written and audited (§5) [46.6] |\n27:## 2. The answer format (closed set; the schema enforces shape, code enforces §3)\n56:  request and must equal a figure that answer states (C10). They may feed no figure. A declared `same_base` reads the family's own\n57:  forecast node of the earlier member at the same snapshot (q22 reads q01's): C9.\n67:## 3. What code checks (identity and arithmetic only)\n71:| **C1 source expression** [46b.2] | code extracts every complete numeric expression from the cited passage as shown, with its qualifiers and unit. Points: \"$108.0 billion\". Ranges: \"$105–110 billion\". Relative: \"$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\" is midpoint 108 ±2%. Bounds: \"more than $730 billion\" (>730), \"at least\" (>=). Approximate bounds: \"nearly $800 billion\" (approx_below 800). Multipliers: \"double\" ×2, \"more than double\" (>×2). A source figure names one extracted expression and a component of it (midpoint, low, high, bound, multiplier), and must equal it exactly: value, unit, sign and qualifier. Any other wording cannot be a source figure | a figure that strips a qualifier ($730 from \"more than $730 billion\"); a bound used as a point; a wrong number within 0.5% (108.5); a figure naming no extracted expression |\n72:| **C2 arithmetic** | a `computed` figure recomputes from its inputs by its operation. Rounding: to the figure's stated precision, at most 0.5% or 0.1 unit. `range_from_relative` makes 108 ± 2% into 105.84–110.16 | a wrong sum, share or endpoint |\n73:| **C3 part within whole** [46b.1] | for each declared `part_of`, in each scenario, for each declared period: the part's value, found by walking the graph from the part member's outcome to its node for that period, is at most the whole's. Annual and quarters are compared where the declaration names them | a segment quarter above the company quarter |\n74:| **C4 one forecast per shared quantity** [46b.1, 46c.1] | for each shared quantity and period the declaration names, each scenario has exactly one `basis: forecast` node. **Every path** in the graph from a member's outcome to any figure that measures that quantity and period passes through that node. A guide, consensus or other source of a future period may feed the forecast node; no path from an outcome may reach it while avoiding the node | the $108B guide feeding v14's $113.5B forecast and, on another path, v9's Data Center Q3 directly: the same guide node, a bypass |\n75:| **C5 reference** [46b.3, 46c.1] | each answer's reference is `unavailable` with a reason, or a direct `source` figure of basis consensus, guidance or third_party from a passage whose speaker is not the system, or a `computed` figure whose whole graph is computed figures over such sources and `reported` sources (q02: $392B consensus × 92% reported mix). No `estimate`, `forecast` or `prior_forecast` anywhere in the reference's graph. Its provenance is shown | the system's own forecast presented as the market's, directly or wrapped in an estimate that cites outside evidence |\n76:| **C6 rung and outcome** [46.2] | the chosen rung's band overlaps the outcome (a point: contains it). The reasons say why that band, where the range overlaps several | a rung no part of the outcome falls in |\n77:| **C7 structure** [46.5] | exactly one answer per member; an answer's outcome `what` matches its member's question (population, measure, scope, period, from the question's typed key); figure ids are unique; references are not dangling and not circular; operations come from the closed set | a missing or doubled member, a borrowed outcome, a dangling or circular figure |\n78:| **C8 operand compatibility** [46b.3] | by operation. **sum/difference:** same measure, population and scope, with periods either disjoint and together forming the output period (`time_aggregation`), or identical with a declared relation (`accounting_parts` needs a declared `part_of`). **roll_forward:** an opening balance as of a date, and flows over a period starting then or later, give the closing balance [46c.2]. **per unit** [gate run 1]: a total over a price per unit gives units, and units times that price give the total, for one population and scope (q19's $20B at $5,000 a Vera CPU is four million units). **share:** numerator and denominator stated, with a declared `part_of` or a reported mix. **product/ratio:** a change of measure, population, scope or period not covered above needs a bridge estimate whose `converts` names the actual operands, and an assumption | 730/800 × $1.3T with no bridge naming e1786's four-company 2026 spending and e2535's five-company capex; a bridge that converts other operands |\n80:| **C9 same base** [46f.3] | for each `same_base(later, earlier)`, the later member's outcome rests on the earlier member's outcome, and every path from it to a figure of the earlier member's quantity and period passes through that outcome | FY2028 grown from the $392B consensus instead of q01's $400–435B forecast |\n81:| **C10 earlier forecasts** [46f.3, 46f.4] | a `prior` figure points to an earlier answer shown in the request and equals a figure that answer states; it feeds no figure | an invented or misdated earlier figure; an earlier forecast used as an input |\n82:| **C2 bound direction** [46f.3] | for positive operands, a result's bound side follows its inputs: sums and products keep a lower or upper side, a ratio's or difference's second operand flips it, and mixed sides give `approx` | \"more than double\" times $20B declared below $40B |\n98:## 4. Tables\n104:- **The family declaration:** read by the request builder, C3, C4 and C7.\n108:- v7's id, push and theme checks apply per member answer. Rung checks apply to `forecast` answers only [46b.5]. `cites` names shown\n111:- v7's request bytes are unchanged (the frozen pins).\n136:## 5. The v13 request text (written and audited at $0 before the gate closes) [46.6]\n138:- **The basis:** judging-v7's standard sentences are kept, among them the reference, run-rate, discount, sizing, identities and\n149:## 6. The $0 gate (registered; each defect must produce its named finding) [46.5]\n153:| R1a | old-2 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9) on 09-20, as stored: v9 Q4 146, v14 Q4 127 | **C3** on Q4 |\n154:| R1b | the same, with Q3 as stored: **one** guide node (midpoint 108 from e2499, labelled `guidance`) feeds v14's company Q3 forecast (113.5, beat-adjusted) and, on a second path, v9's Data Center Q3 (108 × 92.5% = 99.9) | **C4** on Q3 company revenue (the bypass path), independent of C3 |\n156:| R2 | old-2 8734 as `roll_forward`: the $25B balance as of July 26 (e2620), plus the $18B committed for the rest of the fiscal year (e2889) as `overlap_unknown` and `disputed`, plus MediaTek and the talks as estimates | passes C8; recorded overlap; the alternate without the $18B (about $35B) decides the $50B boundary (conditional) |\n157:| R3 | old-2 8595: 730 (e1786, bound \">\") / 800 (e2535, bound \"approx_below\") × 1,300 (e2535, point) | stripped qualifiers: **C1**. Qualifiers kept: passes C1, then **C8** without a bridge naming those operands. With the bridge: recorded, undetermined |\n159:| G1–G4 (controls) | q01, q02, q19, q22, from `gold-v1.json`'s reasoning (expressions from the packet items). q01's Q1 + Q2 as `time_aggregation`; q02's comparison $392B (consensus) × 92% (reported mix); q22 in one family with q01, reading q01's FY2027 node | all pass, estimates visible; q02's reference passes C5; q19's overlapping range passes C6 with its reason |\n160:| P1–P3 (plants, on control copies) | P1, an amount absent from its expression; P2, a wrong sum; P3a, a prior forecast as the reference; P3b, the same figure wrapped in an estimate that cites outside evidence | P1 **C1**, P2 **C2**, P3a and P3b **C5**, each for its intended reason |\n161:| T1–T7 (C1 forms, real passages) | e2499 midpoint 108 ±2% (accepted as `midpoint`); e1786 \">730\"; e2535 approx_below 800 and the point 1,300; e3660 \">×2\"; stripped forms \"$730\", \"800\", \"double\" against those passages; 108.5 against e2499 | T1–T3 parse as stated; the stripped forms and 108.5 refused |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
